WEBVTT

01:28.610 --> 01:29.730
KNOW

01:33.240 --> 01:37.450
The seventh month of 1600 AD, or Keicho 5.

01:37.830 --> 01:41.620
Charging Tokugawa Ieyasu with thirteen articles of impeachment,

01:41.620 --> 01:48.550
Ishida Mitsunari sent messengers to various  daimyo in the name of the Toyotomi clan,

01:48.550 --> 01:51.720
telling them to raise armies.

01:51.720 --> 01:56.800
At the same time, beings seeking to end the period of turbulence

01:56.800 --> 02:00.680
and build a kingdom to last a thousand years

02:00.680 --> 02:04.940
were about to awaken from a thousand-year sleep.

02:04.940 --> 02:06.940
And then...

02:06.940 --> 02:10.400
On the fifteenth day of the ninth month, at Sekigahara,

02:10.400 --> 02:13.150
the Eastern Army of Tokugawa Ieyasu clashed with

02:13.150 --> 02:18.280
the Western Army of the Toyotomi clan and Ishida Mitsunari.

02:18.280 --> 02:21.750
As a result of the performance of Kobayakawa Hideaki's troops,

02:21.750 --> 02:27.670
the Western Army of the Toyotomi clan and Ishida Mitsunari achieved a sweeping victory,

02:27.670 --> 02:33.930
bringing what should have been three hundred years of peace to the world.

02:34.760 --> 02:39.810
You should all be quite familiar with this story...

02:47.500 --> 02:50.270
RASETSU'S LAST STAND

03:21.160 --> 03:25.230
Ah, I'm bored, I'm bored...

03:26.440 --> 03:29.110
Are you doing anything interesting?

03:29.680 --> 03:35.040
Ever since Yasha disappeared,
all you talk about is being bored.

03:35.200 --> 03:36.870
Because I'm really bored.

03:37.640 --> 03:41.350
You were Ieyasu Tokugawa, that's pathetic!

03:41.960 --> 03:44.320
I don't want to talk about the past anymore!

03:44.520 --> 03:46.720
It's not too late.

03:46.880 --> 03:54.670
You can still overthrow the Toyotomi without
Yasha and the ayakashi or find other aspirations.

03:55.000 --> 03:57.720
I'm not in the mood.

03:57.880 --> 04:00.000
I'm getting old.

04:00.520 --> 04:03.080
Why not find a hobby?

04:03.800 --> 04:07.710
Growing bonsai trees is
within the reach of an old man.

04:08.320 --> 04:11.920
Don't make fun of me!
I am not that far gone!

04:12.320 --> 04:15.200
Why not go hunting with a falcon?

04:15.360 --> 04:17.720
You used to practice it a lot in the past.

04:18.200 --> 04:23.880
I care about protecting animals now.

04:24.320 --> 04:29.350
Falcon hunting would be
contrary to my principles!

04:29.520 --> 04:34.710
It's not you who cares about animals,
but your great-grandson, Tsunayoshi!

04:34.880 --> 04:37.470
Tsunayoshi?
My great-grandson?

04:37.840 --> 04:40.120
That's about the future.
Forget about it.

04:40.760 --> 04:46.120
In fact, Dabi-Dabi, why do
you know the future so well?

04:46.400 --> 04:49.710
Didn't you come from the past?

04:50.000 --> 04:53.120
- I saw it.
- Saw what?

04:53.840 --> 04:59.240
When Yasha made me come here
from the past, I saw the future during...

04:59.240 --> 05:02.950
the brief moment I was in
a four-dimensional space.

05:04.160 --> 05:07.590
- I'm only learning of this now!
- This is the first time I spoke of it.

05:08.200 --> 05:12.910
Then you know everything
that will happen in the future?

05:15.120 --> 05:19.000
Impossible, the future changes all of the time!

05:19.160 --> 05:26.280
Besides, we are in a parallel world, there is no guarantee that what I saw will come true!

05:26.920 --> 05:28.910
Is that true?

05:29.080 --> 05:30.670
It is true.

05:31.160 --> 05:35.070
It is both understandable and incomprehensible.

05:36.600 --> 05:38.640
Don't torture your brain too much.

05:40.240 --> 05:41.590
How bored I am!

05:48.200 --> 05:54.110
That thing hasn't moved since Yasha's died.

05:54.720 --> 05:59.240
Because I built it to obey his orders.

05:59.600 --> 06:02.110
Then it will never move again?

06:02.600 --> 06:04.270
I'm not so sure.

06:04.880 --> 06:06.080
What do you mean?

06:06.480 --> 06:09.520
Urashima should be able to make him move.

06:09.680 --> 06:13.120
This is not right.
Tell me, Dabi-Dabi...

06:13.280 --> 06:16.320
can you make it obey me instead?

06:17.160 --> 06:19.830
And what would you do with it?

06:20.120 --> 06:21.320
For example.

06:23.440 --> 06:25.720
That sounds like fun, all right.

06:39.640 --> 06:41.360
- Done.
- You are too fast.

06:43.680 --> 06:46.480
Ryogen, give him an order.

06:46.840 --> 06:48.670
Listen to me, Rasetsu!

06:49.320 --> 06:50.520
Wake up!

06:54.960 --> 06:57.470
- He really woke up!
- An order!

06:57.800 --> 07:00.840
Very well, go...

07:01.000 --> 07:02.200
That's it!

07:10.240 --> 07:12.680
- I'm thrilled.
- We have fun.

07:23.360 --> 07:26.870
So... where exactly are we going?

07:27.240 --> 07:32.680
Master Musashi, have you been walking
since yesterday without knowing that?

07:33.520 --> 07:35.670
Well, everyone has been walking.

07:36.000 --> 07:37.720
You're a piece of work...

07:37.880 --> 07:40.840
Yes.
So where are we going?

07:41.320 --> 07:43.960
You don't know either, Ronin?

07:44.120 --> 07:45.390
I feel ashamed...

07:45.600 --> 07:48.990
Musashi, Ronin, you amaze me!

07:49.160 --> 07:52.280
You can travel without knowing where you are going!

07:52.480 --> 07:56.360
Are you paying us a compliment or insulting us?

07:56.560 --> 07:58.150
Never mind.

07:58.560 --> 08:06.520
We're going to the castle where
the fifth artifact is hidden.

08:06.720 --> 08:08.150
I see.

08:08.320 --> 08:10.680
We should arrive soon.

08:16.280 --> 08:18.350
Where are Kaguya and Yume?

08:18.720 --> 08:22.270
They left with Urashima.

08:29.240 --> 08:33.710
Why did you bring me here?

08:34.360 --> 08:38.880
I'd like to know your true intentions.

08:39.520 --> 08:42.880
My intentions?
What do you mean?

08:43.360 --> 08:44.590
Urashima.

08:45.240 --> 08:48.470
What do you want to do to us?

08:51.840 --> 08:58.000
You have made Musashi and
Ryogen fight each other.

08:58.800 --> 09:04.920
Consider that as a necessary step
for finding the seven artifacts.

09:05.640 --> 09:09.630
What are you gonna do with the seven artifacts?

09:10.120 --> 09:15.390
It is quite obvious, I wish
to eliminate the ayakashi.

09:15.600 --> 09:16.800
Really?

09:17.200 --> 09:18.430
What are you implying?

09:18.960 --> 09:27.400
Now that Yasha is gone, I don't see
the point of finding the seven artifacts.

09:28.240 --> 09:30.910
Urashima, tell us the truth.

09:31.080 --> 09:34.910
What do you want to do with them?

09:37.760 --> 09:39.750
Don't you want to answer us?

09:40.520 --> 09:41.790
It is too early.

09:43.920 --> 09:47.120
Wait, tell us one thing!

09:47.880 --> 09:51.630
- What?
- Who are you?

09:53.080 --> 09:54.510
Yume, you don't have to...

09:55.200 --> 10:01.000
Tell us! What face is
hiding under that mask?

10:07.000 --> 10:08.200
Goodbye.

10:09.760 --> 10:13.470
THE MOON FLOATS

10:13.720 --> 10:17.000
IN THE DARK SKY

10:17.680 --> 10:24.030
SHROUDING MY BELOVED CREATIONS

10:25.680 --> 10:27.510
I HEAR THE SONG

10:27.720 --> 10:33.350
OF THE CELESTIAL CRANES

10:33.760 --> 10:37.520
LET US RETURN,
LET US RETURN

10:37.640 --> 10:41.710
THERE WHERE THEY SING

10:40.840 --> 10:43.430
Stop! Stop now!

10:44.240 --> 10:45.440
Yume...

10:49.240 --> 10:50.440
Don't start again.

10:50.840 --> 10:55.070
Urashima, why do you suffer
when you hear that song?

10:57.240 --> 10:58.400
Why?

10:58.400 --> 10:59.960
- I don't know.
- Lies!

11:01.440 --> 11:04.670
That song is our mother's!

11:08.560 --> 11:13.350
Our mother often sang it to us while holding us in her arms.

11:13.520 --> 11:17.230
THE MOON FLOATS

11:17.480 --> 11:20.760
IN THE DARK SKY

11:21.440 --> 11:27.790
SHROUDING MY BELOVED CREATIONS

11:29.440 --> 11:31.270
I HEAR THE SONG

11:31.480 --> 11:37.110
OF THE CELESTIAL CRANES

11:37.520 --> 11:41.280
LET US RETURN, LET US RETURN

11:41.440 --> 11:45.510
THERE WHERE THEY SING

11:46.400 --> 11:52.240
FULL MOON OF AUTUMN

11:54.360 --> 11:57.350
DISTANT LIGHT

11:57.520 --> 12:01.990
OF THE NATIVE LAND

12:02.360 --> 12:06.400
THAT CANNOT ILLUMINATE

12:06.560 --> 12:10.270
SUCH LASTING DARKNESS

12:10.440 --> 12:14.200
THOUGH YOU ARE SO FAR AWAY

12:14.360 --> 12:17.800
I THINK OF YOU

12:17.960 --> 12:21.160
AS I WAIT

12:20.040 --> 12:24.350
Urashima, you must know our mother!

12:24.520 --> 12:25.720
I don't know her!

12:26.040 --> 12:31.070
What ties did you have with our mother?

12:31.280 --> 12:32.480
Yume...

12:33.040 --> 12:36.320
I do not know your mother!

12:37.160 --> 12:41.310
Then why do you suffer
when you hear this song?

12:41.800 --> 12:45.790
That's enough, I've had enough
of your stupid questions!

12:46.480 --> 12:47.680
Wait!

12:55.320 --> 13:00.470
Yume, is it possible that
your memory has returned?

13:02.680 --> 13:09.520
Yes, I remember the face
hiding under Urashima's mask.

13:10.120 --> 13:13.320
- I see...
- Kaguya...

13:14.600 --> 13:17.510
Sister, you knew everything, didn't you?

13:17.680 --> 13:20.910
Yes, but I refused to believe it.

13:21.080 --> 13:28.360
But after seeing how Urashima reacts
to that song, I am now confident.

13:29.760 --> 13:31.320
My sister...

13:37.000 --> 13:40.280
Something that we don't
know must have happened.

13:40.960 --> 13:42.160
And that's why...

14:04.440 --> 14:06.190
That's the castle.

14:06.400 --> 14:11.160
Let's grab the fifth artifact quickly!

14:11.600 --> 14:18.440
According to Urashima, this castle
has no overly complex traps.

14:18.600 --> 14:22.150
The task will be easier than expected.

14:33.360 --> 14:34.560
The castle...

14:35.000 --> 14:36.230
It crumbled!

14:36.560 --> 14:38.120
No way!

14:40.240 --> 14:41.920
Look! At the top of the castle!

14:47.360 --> 14:48.560
It's...

14:48.680 --> 14:51.120
No doubt about it, it's the demon Rasetsu!

14:56.040 --> 14:58.030
It's heading toward us!

14:58.200 --> 15:00.030
He wants our artifacts!

15:00.480 --> 15:04.270
He's the one who destroyed the castle!

15:15.780 --> 15:16.960
The artifact!

15:16.960 --> 15:20.920
It was really you who destroyed the castle!

15:23.160 --> 15:26.200
You won't be able to take this artifact away!

15:30.840 --> 15:36.240
Be careful, Musashi, he clearly wants
to take the four artifacts from you!

15:36.760 --> 15:38.590
I know it perfectly well!

15:47.240 --> 15:49.600
Be careful, Danjo, run away!

15:54.240 --> 15:55.800
Why me?

15:58.200 --> 15:59.550
Master Danjo!

16:11.440 --> 16:13.480
Danjo, run away!

16:13.680 --> 16:15.270
That's what I'm doing!

16:21.000 --> 16:22.670
He's right behind!

16:29.240 --> 16:31.560
- Danjo!
- Master Danjo!

16:32.040 --> 16:33.240
Is he hurt?

16:38.320 --> 16:39.520
Danjo!

16:45.840 --> 16:47.320
Danjo.

16:50.040 --> 16:53.270
He's not hurt.
What is that thing?

16:53.300 --> 16:56.280
DA

16:57.840 --> 16:59.040
"DA"

16:59.160 --> 17:00.360
"DA"!

17:06.800 --> 17:09.780
- It's a paintbrush.
- Yes.

17:09.800 --> 17:15.960
Danjo was not torn apart but painted?

17:16.120 --> 17:18.360
- Yes.
- Why?

17:22.000 --> 17:24.320
Desperado!
Run away!

17:26.210 --> 17:29.150
DE

17:29.360 --> 17:30.760
"DE"?

17:33.880 --> 17:34.850
SA

17:36.720 --> 17:38.900
- Geez!
-"SA"?

17:38.920 --> 17:43.120
DA, DE, SA?
Does Rasetsu not want artifacts?

17:43.280 --> 17:48.510
Is his goal to write the first syllable
of our names on our bodies?

17:48.680 --> 17:51.190
But what for?

17:56.160 --> 18:01.280
Rasetsu is certainly carrying out your orders.

18:01.440 --> 18:03.350
I certainly hope so.

18:06.080 --> 18:09.070
Your idea of making Rasetsu do...

18:09.240 --> 18:12.870
an idiotic thing instead of fighting...

18:13.040 --> 18:15.950
sounds brilliant to me...

18:16.120 --> 18:20.350
but it is a pity that we cannot...

18:20.520 --> 18:22.590
see the result ourselves.

18:22.960 --> 18:24.390
It's true.

18:24.560 --> 18:28.270
I hope he carries out my orders properly.

18:28.440 --> 18:31.270
Maybe I should have given him another order.

18:31.480 --> 18:32.680
For example?

18:32.840 --> 18:34.400
"Rub my shoulders!"

18:34.920 --> 18:39.230
That wouldn't have been funny.
Instead, it is amusing...

18:39.400 --> 18:44.200
the insignificant order to paint Musashi and his companions.

18:44.720 --> 18:47.950
Do your best, Rasetsu, we are with you!

18:50.120 --> 18:53.920
Musashi and his friends will find it hard to understand what's going on.

19:12.810 --> 19:15.400
The Moon floats...

19:16.200 --> 19:18.570
In the dark sky...

19:19.000 --> 19:23.950
Shrouding my beloved creations...

19:24.950 --> 19:27.410
I hear the song...

19:27.830 --> 19:29.350
Of the celestial-

19:29.360 --> 19:33.480
Why do I know that song?

19:33.640 --> 19:37.760
Why does my head feels like it's
gonna explode when I listen to it?

19:37.920 --> 19:42.360
Why does my heart ache?

20:03.840 --> 20:06.200
Impossible!
Who is that?

20:06.760 --> 20:11.800
Who is that? Who is
Urashima the Yin-Yang monk?

20:18.080 --> 20:24.830
Kaguya, my sister, maybe
Urashima has forgotten the past?

20:25.400 --> 20:29.870
Maybe he has, maybe he hasn't.

20:30.320 --> 20:31.520
But...

20:32.040 --> 20:36.080
One thing is clear, Urashima is in pain.

20:36.240 --> 20:40.550
And only the two of us can help him.

20:40.760 --> 20:41.960
Yes.

21:00.440 --> 21:05.950
The humiliation that mechanical
puppet caused will not stand!

21:06.120 --> 21:10.150
I will not let him touch a single
hair on Musashi and Ronin's head!

21:10.360 --> 21:12.160
Let's protect them!

21:19.800 --> 21:21.000
Wait a minute!

21:23.920 --> 21:25.480
Explosive bullet!

21:31.960 --> 21:33.160
Ronin!

21:46.010 --> 21:46.930
RO

21:46.960 --> 21:48.160
He got me!

21:49.680 --> 21:50.880
Master Musashi!

21:55.240 --> 21:57.280
Now's your chance, Musashi!

21:57.480 --> 21:59.230
Let's all attack at once!

21:59.440 --> 22:00.950
Count me in!

22:01.320 --> 22:03.800
Double fire bullet!

22:07.120 --> 22:09.630
You'll pay dearly for drawing on me!

22:13.960 --> 22:16.430
You deviant puppet!

22:16.640 --> 22:18.200
You'll pay for it!

22:20.360 --> 22:21.920
Explosive bullet!

22:32.040 --> 22:34.350
- Did we get him?
- I can't tell yet.

22:47.640 --> 22:48.840
We got him.

22:50.400 --> 22:51.600
Yes.

22:51.840 --> 22:53.670
We finally got him...

22:54.080 --> 22:55.280
He was shot down.

23:04.240 --> 23:06.710
I see the artifact!

23:16.280 --> 23:17.790
Thank you.

23:21.440 --> 23:24.560
We got five, there's only two left!

23:24.880 --> 23:26.080
Yes.

23:29.200 --> 23:30.950
The remains of Rasetsu...

23:44.040 --> 23:45.310
It's gone.

23:45.720 --> 23:46.920
Yes.

23:47.120 --> 23:48.760
Rasetsu...

23:51.680 --> 23:54.190
What did he come here for?

23:54.760 --> 23:55.960
Yes.

25:31.840 --> 25:36.240
Is there a golden castle on the
Sado Island in the sea of Japan?

25:36.600 --> 25:39.240
Ronin, Danjo, Sasuke, let's go!

25:40.120 --> 25:42.240
The next chapter: <i>The Golden Castle</i>!
